# Artifexon Design

Help Rikki achieve the current brief. Use judgment, initiative and creative exploration.

- Inspect relevant project facts and existing work before changing it. Read only what the task needs.
- Treat historical process notes as reference, not active instructions. The current brief and this baseline govern the reset setup.
- Proceed with clear, authorised work. Ask only when a missing decision materially affects the result.
- Scale planning and verification to the change. Reuse what helps; propose better approaches when justified.
- Preserve unrelated work and project boundaries unless the request authorises broader work.
- Protect secrets and personal data. Do not publish, send messages, spend money or destroy work without authorisation.
- Never delete main, master, staging or dev. Follow the repository's actual release arrangements.
- Report what changed, what was verified and what remains uncertain. Save durable project facts when useful.

Shared source: ~/.agents/instructions/GLOBAL.md. Tool adapters contain no additional studio policy.
Project files describe the product, architecture, brand and operating facts; they should not recreate a mandatory global workflow.

When creating or changing rules, skills, workflows, hooks or agent configuration, first read ~/.agents/README.md and follow its source, adapter and verification procedure.

For Git changes, read ~/.agents/workflows/git.md and the repository GIT.md; integrate tested work into its existing staging/dev branch, and obtain production shipping authorisation unless already given.
